## Her Signature Nail Shape (And Why It Matters)

An oval nail shape is a rounded, tapered form with soft edges and no flat tip, the consistent shape behind every version of Hadid's manicure. It is not interchangeable with square, almond, or coffin. Oval softens the whole hand, and it is the shape choice that lets a sheer polish read as natural rather than styled.

Shape does more work here than people expect from something this understated. A sharp square tip paired with a translucent nude can look unfinished. An oval tip paired with the same sheer polish looks complete, because the rounded edge already suggests care, so the colour reads as a finishing touch rather than the only effort made.

