## How to Recreate the Look at Home

Sheer nude nails at home come down to thin, translucent layers over a clean, buffed nail rather than one heavy coat, and the technique is genuinely simple enough to do without salon equipment. The entire process runs under an hour, start to finish, and needs no gel curing lamp unless you specifically choose a gel formula.

Start with the shape. File to oval, softening any flat edges. Buff the surface lightly, just enough to remove ridges so the polish sits smoothly. Push back cuticles and apply a thin layer of cuticle oil, letting it absorb fully. Apply your chosen sheer mocha or nude polish in two to three thin coats, letting each dry before the next. Resist loading the brush heavily. Thin is the entire technique. Finish with a high-gloss top coat, which does most of the work in making the manicure look finished.

